|info     =
*Zephyr launches a rapidly traveling slice of dense air towards her aiming reticle, expending {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''50''' [[energy]] while grounded or {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''25''' energy while airborne. Upon colliding with a surface or travelling its maximum distance of <u>'''100'''</u> meters, the slice explodes in a {{Stat|Ability Range|icon=only}}'''4 / 5 / 7 / 8 ''' meters radius, inflicting {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''200 / 300 / 400 / 500''' damage distributed between {{D|Impact}}, {{D|Puncture}}, and {{D|Slash}} damage with a <u>'''50%'''</u> [[Status Chance]], as well as {{D|Knockdown}} and {{D|Ragdoll}}. Each enemy hit directly by the slice or by the subsequent explosion radius will increase Airburst's damage by +<u>'''35%'''</u> for subsequent hits.
**'''Tap''' the ability key (default {{Keybind|2}}) to pull enemies towards the center of the blast. '''Hold''' down the ability key to push enemies away instead.
***Airburst's pull force lingers for <u>'''2'''</u> seconds on the surface it collides with, during which the affected enemies remain ragdolled and gradually slide toward the center.
**The <u>'''35%'''</u> damage increase is additive per hit, for a total damage increase of +35% after 1 hit, +70% after 2 hits, etc. 
***The bonus accumulated from direct hits will carry over to the explosion.
***The explosion will hit all enemies within its range at the same time, but the hits will be registered one at a time (in order of the enemies' distance from the explosion). This allows the damage bonus to stack up for each enemy hit. For example, hitting 3 enemies with just the explosion will cause the nearest enemy to take 500 damage, the next closest to take 500 * 1.35 = 675, and the furthest to take 500 * 1.70 = 850.
**Damage distribution is '''20%''' {{D|Impact}}, '''10%''' {{D|Puncture}}, and '''70%''' {{D|Slash}}.
**Airburst projectiles have innate [[punch through]] and can bypass certain objects in the environment (e.g. closed doors).
*The explosion can damage objects and enemies through walls and other cover, bypassing [[Line of Sight]].
*Casting Airburst is a [[One-Handed Action]], meaning it can be used while performing many actions without interrupting them, including [[reload]]ing, charging, shooting, and moving (either [[Maneuvers#Sprinting|sprinting]] or [[Maneuvers#Sliding|sliding]]).
*Subsuming Zephyr to the [[Helminth]] will offer Airburst and its augments to be used by other Warframes.
**Subsumed Airburst includes the tap-cast for wind vacuum and hold-cast for wind explosion.
*Direct hits from the projectile benefit from {{M|Vigorous Swap}} and other modifiers that affect abilities that deal "weapon damage", including damage boosting abilities such as {{A|Eclipse}}.
